From a979e2487a280929e8083a6ff65aa7e7f9d37fe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasiliy Yorkin <vasiliy.yorkin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:07:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: forward direct keybindings to panes that want them

A direct (prefix-free) binding belongs to Herdr, so the program inside the
pane never sees that chord. Full-screen editors and pagers lose their own
ctrl+letter chords as soon as a user maps one, and Herdr had no way to hand
a chord back the way tmux's @pane-is-vim does.

Add keys.direct_keys with three values: herdr keeps every direct binding
(the default, so nothing changes for existing configs), auto forwards them
while the focused pane's application is on the alternate screen, and pane
always forwards them. herdr pane direct-keys sets the same choice for one
pane and is served by a new pane.direct_keys.set method, so the published
pane.input.set shape stays untouched. Prefix mode is unaffected.

The client decides per keypress, so a pane that enters or leaves the
alternate screen switches over on the next chord with no reload.
